<h2 id="adding-user-interaction-prompting-for-confirmation" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Adding User Interaction: Prompting for Confirmation</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#adding-user-interaction-prompting-for-confirmation" aria-label="Link to Adding User Interaction: Prompting for Confirmation"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>Before we automatically create a Neon branch, we might want to ask the user if they want to create one. We can do this with the <code>sh</code> read command:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full" data-has-filename="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="bash"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-comment)">#!/bin/sh</span></span>
