<span class="line" data-line="3"><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">  BRANCH_NAME</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">=</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">$(</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)">git</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> symbolic-ref</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> --short</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> HEAD</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">)</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="4"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)">  read</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> -p</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string-expression)"> &quot;Do you want to create a Neon branch for $BRANCH_NAME? (y/n): &quot;</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> answer</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> &lt;</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)">/dev/tty</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="5"></span>
<span class="line" data-line="6"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-comment)">  # further code...</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="7"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">fi</span></span></code></pre><button class="invisible absolute right-4 border border-gray-new-80 bg-white p-1.5 text-gray-new-40 opacity-0 transition-[background-color,opacity,visibility] duration-200 group-hover/code-block:visible group-hover/code-block:opacity-100 hover:bg-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:bg-black-pure dark:text-gray-new-60 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8 lg:visible lg:opacity-100 top-4" type="button" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-current"><rect width="8.995" height="9.002" x="5.939" y="5.935" stroke="currentColor" rx="1"></rect><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.434.935a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5 1.5v7.001a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.5 1.5h1.499a.5.5 0 0 0 0-1h-1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V2.435a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h6.995a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v1.5a.5.5 0 1 0 1 0v-1.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></figure>
<p>Here, the read command reads the user’s input into the answer variable. However, it’s important to note that Githooks are not connected to the terminal, so we have to redirect input from /dev/tty.</p>
